    document.getElementById("container").innerHTML='<div class="background-container-GPW-BoM"><div class="black"><div class="fade-out-simple"></div><p class="hidden-text-left" style="transform:translate(0,-30px);">The Persian fleet landed at Marathon, about 40 kilometers from Athens, where the Athenian army, led by Miltiades, blocked their path. After a five-day stalemate, the Persians began to load their troops back onto the ships. Seizing the opportunity, the Athenians descended from the hills and attacked, routing the weaker Persian soldiers and causing them to flee. The Greeks suffered minimal losses while inflicting heavy casualties on the Persians. With the Persian survivors retreating to their ships, the Athenians quickly marched back to Athens, preventing further Persian advances. The Battle of Marathon marked a turning point in the Greco-Persian Wars, demonstrating that the Persians could be defeated and showcasing the effectiveness of heavily armored Greek hoplites.</p><div class="fade-in-simple" style="transform:translate(0,-65px);"></div></div></div><div class="main-container"></div>'
