    document.getElementById("container").innerHTML='<div class="background-container-PW-defeat"><div class="black"><div class="fade-out-simple"></div><p class="hidden-text-left" style="transform:translate(0,-30px);">Following a Spartan victory at the naval battle of Notium in 406 BC, Alcibiades, a prominent Athenian leader, fell out of favor and exiled himself from the city. Athens later won the naval battle of Arginusae but failed to rescue stranded crews, leading to outrage and the controversial execution of six naval commanders. With its navy weakened and morale low, Athens faced a decisive blow at the Battle of Aegospotami in 405 BC, where the Spartan fleet, led by the skilled general Lysander, destroyed most of the Athenian ships. Facing starvation and disease, Athens surrendered in 404 BC, losing its walls, fleet, and overseas territories. While some urged for Athens destruction, the Spartans spared the city, incorporating it into their system and granting it leniency due to its past contributions to Greeces defense.</p><div class="fade-in-simple" style="transform:translate(0,-89px);"></div></div></div><div class="main-container"></div>'
